-- title:
--   Finitely many ratios carry a non-zero window product
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $K$ and $L$ are number fields with $L/K$ a finite Galois extension, $\sigma : L \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K]} L$ is an automorphism such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$ (hypothesis `hgen`), and $[L:K] = \operatorname{finrank}_K L$ is prime (hypothesis `hprime`). A Haar measure $\nu_{Z_K}$ on the unit group $(\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$ of the adele ring of $K$ is fixed, for the Borel measurable structure of its topology. Two finite sets $S_K, T$ of finite places of $K$ (height-one primes of $\mathcal{O}_K$) are fixed, with $T$ disjoint from $S_K$ (`hTS`).
--
--   For $u \in K^\times$ and $z \in (\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$ write $\gamma(u,z) = \mathrm{scalar}(z)\cdot \mathrm{diag}(u,1) \in GL_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, the element `centralScalar (𝓞 K) K z * diagUnits2 (Units.map (algebraMap K (AdeleRing (𝓞 K) K)) u) 1`, i.e. the diagonal matrix with entries $zu$ and $z$, $u$ being transported to $\mathbb{A}_K$ by the structure map; write $\gamma_\infty(u,z) =$ `AdelicLevel.glArch (𝓞 K) K` of it, its archimedean component, and $\gamma_v(u,z) =$ `AdelicLevel.finComponent (𝓞 K) K v (AdelicLevel.glFin (𝓞 K) K …)`, its component at a finite place $v$.
--
--   *Test data.* A function $f_{a,K}$ on $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_{K,\infty})$ which is an archimedean test factor (`hfaK`: it is $\Phi$ composed with the matrix of archimedean entries for some $C^\infty$ function $\Phi$ on $2\times 2$ matrices over the mixed space of $K$, and has compact support); functions $f_{S_K,v}$ on $GL_2(K_v)$ which for $v \in S_K$ are locally constant with compact support (`hfSK`); an archimedean test factor $\varphi_a$ on $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_{L,\infty})$ in the same sense for $L$ (`hφa`); functions $\varphi_{S,v}$ on $GL_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ which for $v \in S_K$ are locally constant with compact support (`hφS`); and functions $f_{T,v}$ on $GL_2(K_v)$ which for $v \in T$ are locally constant with compact support (`hfT`).
--
--   *Global factorisation.* A measure $\nu_A$ on $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_{K,\infty})$ for the Borel structure `glBorelOf`, and a real constant $c_G$ subject to `hG`: for every finite set $S$ of finite places, every $f$ on $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, every $f_a$ on $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_{K,\infty})$ and every family $f_S$ of functions on the $GL_2(K_v)$, if $f_a$ is a.e. strongly measurable for $\nu_A$, each $f_S(v)$ ($v \in S$) is a.e. strongly measurable for the local Haar measure `localHaar K v`, $f(g) = f_a(\gamma\text{-arch component of }g)\cdot\prod_{v \in S} f_S(v)(g_v)$ whenever all components $g_v$ with $v \notin S$ lie in the integral set `localIntegralSet K v` (matrices over $\mathcal{O}_v$ with inverse over $\mathcal{O}_v$), and $f(g) = 0$ whenever some component $g_v$ with $v \notin S$ lies outside that set, then $\int f \, d(\mathrm{adelicGLHaar}) = c_G \cdot (\int f_a \, d\nu_A) \cdot \prod_{v \in S} \int f_S(v)\, d(\mathrm{localHaar}\,K\,v)$.
--
--   *Centraliser measures and their factorisation.* A constant $c_{\tau K} > 0$; measures $\tau_G(u,z)$ on the centraliser of $\{\gamma(u,z)\}$ in $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, which are Haar measures whenever $u \neq 1$ in $K$ (`hτG`) and satisfy the diagonal evaluation `hτGc`: for $u \neq 1$ and every $g : GL_2(\mathbb{A}_K) \to \mathbb{C}$, $\int_{\mathrm{Cent}} g(t)\, d\tau_G(u,z) = c_{\tau K}\int g(\mathrm{diag}(p_1,p_2))\, d(\nu_{Z_K}\times\nu_{Z_K})$. Measures $\tau_A(u,z)$ on the centraliser of $\{\gamma_\infty(u,z)\}$ in $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_{K,\infty})$, Haar for $u \neq 1$ (`hτA`); measures $\tau_F(u,z,v)$ on the local centraliser of $\gamma_v(u,z)$ in $GL_2(K_v)$, Haar for $u \neq 1$ (`hτF`) and of total mass $1$ on the preimage of `localIntegralSet K v` (`hτF1`). A constant $c_T > 0$ and the factorisation `hT`: for $u \neq 1$, $z$, a finite set $S$, a function $W$ on the centraliser of $\{\gamma(u,z)\}$, a function $W_a$ on $GL_2(\mathbb{A}_{K,\infty})$ and a family $W_S$, if $W_a$ is a.e. strongly measurable for $\tau_A(u,z)$, each $W_S(v)$ ($v \in S$) is a.e. strongly measurable for $\tau_F(u,z,v)$, $W(t)$ factors as $W_a$ of the archimedean component times $\prod_{v \in S} W_S(v)$ of the $v$-components for those $t$ all of whose components outside $S$ are integral, and $W(t) = 0$ when some component of $t$ outside $S$ is not integral, then $\int W \, d\tau_G(u,z) = c_T\,(\int W_a\, d\tau_A(u,z))\prod_{v\in S}\int W_S(v)\, d\tau_F(u,z,v)$.
--
--   *Untwisted orbital integrals.* Families $I_A, I_F, J_A, J_F$ of complex numbers, indexed by $u \in K^\times$, $z \in (\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$ and (for $I_F, J_F$) a finite place, such that for $u \neq 1$: $I_A(u,z)$ is an orbital integral of $f_{a,K}$ at $\gamma_\infty(u,z)$ for $\nu_A$ and $\tau_A(u,z)$, i.e. $I_A(u,z) = \int f_{a,K}(x^{-1}\gamma_\infty x)\,w(x)\,d\nu_A$ for some non-negative measurable compactly supported $w$ whose $\tau_A$-average along the centraliser is $1$ at every $x$ where the integrand does not vanish (`hIA`); for $v \in S_K$, $I_F(u,z,v)$ is the corresponding local orbital integral of $f_{S_K,v}$ at $\gamma_v(u,z)$ for `localHaar K v` and $\tau_F(u,z,v)$ (`hIF`); $J_A(u,z)$ is a weighted orbital integral of $f_{a,K}$ at $\gamma_\infty(u,z)$ in the same sense, with weight $y \mapsto -\log \mathrm{archHeight}_K(y) - \log \mathrm{archHeight}_K(\mathrm{glArch}(\mathrm{adelicWeyl}_K)\,y)$, where $\mathrm{adelicWeyl}$ is the image of the Weyl element $\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\1&0\end{pmatrix}$ and $\mathrm{archHeight}$ is the product over infinite places of the local heights $|\det|/\mathrm{rowNormSq}$ raised to the multiplicity (`hJA`); and for $v \in S_K$, $J_F(u,z,v)$ is the local weighted orbital integral of $f_{S_K,v}$ at $\gamma_v(u,z)$ with the local weight (`hJF`).
--
--   *Twisted side.* A measure $\nu_A'$ on $GL_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_{K,\infty})$ for `glBorelOf`, with the normalisations $\nu_A = \mathrm{archHaarK}\,K$ and $\nu_A' = \mathrm{archHaarL}\,K\,L$ (`hνA`, `hνA'`). A family $\delta_A(u,z) \in GL_2(L\otimes_K\mathbb{A}_{K,\infty})$ such that for $u \neq 1$, whenever $\gamma_\infty(u,z)$ is a norm (that is, some $\delta$ satisfies $\mathrm{toTensorGL}(\gamma_\infty) = y^{-1}\,\mathrm{normString}(\delta)\,y$ for some $y$, where $\mathrm{normString}(\delta) = \prod_{i<[L:K]}\sigma_{GL}^{i}(\delta)$), the norm string of $\delta_A(u,z)$ equals $\mathrm{toTensorGL}(\gamma_\infty(u,z))$ (`hδA`); measures $\tau_A'(u,z)$ on the $\sigma$-twisted centraliser $\{t : t\,\delta_A(u,z)\,\sigma_{GL}(t)^{-1} = \delta_A(u,z)\}$, Haar for $u \neq 1$ (`hτA'`), and coupled to $\tau_A(u,z)$ with conjugator $1$ when a norm exists (`hτA'c`: the pushforward of $\tau_A'(u,z)$ under $t \mapsto t$ equals the pushforward of $\tau_A(u,z)$ under $\mathrm{toTensorGL}$). Likewise a family $\delta_F(u,z,v) \in GL_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$ whose norm string equals $\mathrm{toTensorGL}(\gamma_v(u,z))$ for $u \neq 1$, $v \in S_K$ and $\gamma_v(u,z)$ a norm (`hδF`); measures $\tau_F'(u,z,v)$ on the twisted centraliser of $\delta_F(u,z,v)$, Haar for $u \neq 1$ (`hτF'`) and of mass $1$ on the preimage of `semiLocalIntegralSet K L v` (`hτF'1`). Families $J_A'$ and $J_F'$ such that for $u \neq 1$: if $\gamma_\infty(u,z)$ is a norm then $J_A'(u,z)$ is a twisted weighted orbital integral of $\varphi_a \circ \mathrm{archIdentGL}$ at $\delta_A(u,z)$ for $\nu_A'$ and $\tau_A'(u,z)$, with weight $y \mapsto -\log \mathrm{archHeight}_L(\mathrm{archIdentGL}(y)) - \log\mathrm{archHeight}_L(\mathrm{glArch}(\mathrm{adelicWeyl}_L)\,\mathrm{archIdentGL}(y))$ (`hJA'`), and if it is not a norm then $J_A'(u,z) = 0$ (`hJA'0`); and for $v \in S_K$, $J_F'(u,z,v)$ is the twisted weighted orbital integral of $\varphi_{S,v}$ at $\delta_F(u,z,v)$ for the semilocal Haar measure, semilocal weight and $\tau_F'(u,z,v)$ when $\gamma_v(u,z)$ is a norm (`hJF'`), and $J_F'(u,z,v) = 0$ otherwise (`hJF'0`).
--
--   *Auxiliary places.* A family $I_T(u,z,v)$ which for $u \neq 1$ and $v \in T$ is the local orbital integral of $f_{T,v}$ at $\gamma_v(u,z)$ for $\tau_F(u,z,v)$ (`hIT`), and a family $I_U(u,z,v)$ which for $u \neq 1$ and $v \notin S_K \cup T$ is the local orbital integral at $\gamma_v(u,z)$ of the indicator function of `localIntegralSet K v` (`hIU`).
--
--   Under these hypotheses there exists a finite subset $U \subseteq K^\times$ such that for every $u \in K^\times$ with $u \notin U$ and $u \neq 1$ in $K$, and every $z \in (\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$,
--   $$\Big(\prod_{v \in T} I_T(u,z,v)\Big)\cdot\Big(\prod_{v \notin S_K \cup T}^{\mathrm{f}} I_U(u,z,v)\Big)\cdot\Big[\big(J_A'(u,z) - [L:K]\,J_A(u,z)\big)\prod_{v \in S_K} I_F(u,z,v) + I_A(u,z)\sum_{v \in S_K}\big(J_F'(u,z,v) - [L:K]\,J_F(u,z,v)\big)\prod_{v' \in S_K \setminus \{v\}} I_F(u,z,v')\Big] = 0,$$
--   where the second factor is the finite product (`finprod`) of $I_U(u,z,v)$ over the places $v$ outside $S_K \cup T$, the coefficient $[L:K]$ is $\operatorname{finrank}_K L$ viewed in $\mathbb{C}$, and the inner product in the sum runs over $S_K$ with $v$ erased.
--
--   This is the finiteness step in the comparison of hyperbolic terms for cyclic base change of prime degree for $GL(2)$: away from a finite set of ratios $u$, the window expression built from the split-family orbital and weighted orbital integrals (twisted minus $[L:K]$ times untwisted, at the archimedean place and at the places of $S_K$, multiplied by the contributions at $T$ and the unit contributions elsewhere) vanishes identically in the central parameter $z$. It is used in the assembly of the winding identity that expresses the hyperbolic intercept as a Satake-type sum over the finitely many surviving ratios.
